Article 1-2 (Duties)
The Defense Intelligence Headquarters (hereinafter referred to as the "Intelligence Headquarters") shall perform the following duties: [Amended on July 1, 2011 and April 7, 2026.]
1. Integrating and coordinating defense intelligence policies and planning;
2. Assessing international situations and collecting, analyzing, producing, and disseminating overseas military intelligence;
3. Collecting, analyzing, producing, and disseminating military strategic intelligence;
4. Providing intelligence support necessary for military diplomacy and the defense industry;
5. Dispatching and managing military attachés stationed at diplomatic missions abroad;
6. Cooperating with foreign military attachés stationed in the Republic of Korea and exchanging intelligence with foreign countries;
7. Requesting appropriations for and administering budgets for special military intelligence under the jurisdiction of the Intelligence Headquarters;
8. Managing military security, including cybersecurity, and policies on defense-industry security;
9. Developing military intelligence capabilities;
10. Conducting affairs concerning military technical intelligence;
11. Conducting affairs concerning military-related geospatial information (including imagery information; hereinafter the same shall apply) and meteorological information;
12. Performing other duties related to military intelligence.
